namespace jo.jvm

import jo.compile.intrinsic

//[ Bind a Jo function directly to a JVM/JDK member, bypassing normal compilation.
  !
  ! This is the FFI mechanism for the JVM backend: it lets a small number of
  ! trusted declarations in `jo.jvm.runtime` (and, in the future, user code)
  ! reach into the JDK class library without the compiler needing built-in
  ! knowledge of every JDK symbol.
  !
  ! - `owner`  the JVM internal class name, e.g. "java/io/PrintStream"
  ! - `member` the field/method name on the JVM side; "<init>" for constructors
  ! - `desc`   the JVM descriptor for the member, e.g. "(I)Ljava/lang/String;"
  ! - `kind`   selects the shape of the generated bytecode:
  !
  !     "static"    invokestatic;   every Jo param is a call argument
  !     "virtual"   invokevirtual;  first Jo param is the receiver
  !     "interface" invokeinterface; first Jo param is the receiver
  !     "special"   `new owner; dup; <args>; invokespecial owner.<init>:desc`
  !     "getstatic" read a static field; the Jo function takes no params
  !     "putstatic" write a static field; the single Jo param is the value
  !     "getfield"  read an instance field; the Jo param is the receiver
  !     "putfield"  write an instance field; params are (receiver, value)
  !
  ! The body of an `@extern`-annotated function is never compiled — the
  ! backend recognizes the annotation before attempting to compile a call,
  ! and emits the described instruction(s) directly. Write a placeholder
  ! body such as `= ...` (uncalled).
  !
  ! Named `jo.jvm.extern` — scoped under `jvm` since it's specific to this
  ! backend (a future native/wasm/... backend would want its own extern
  ! mechanism, not this one), and named `extern` rather than reusing `jvm`
  ! itself so it doesn't collide with `jvm` as a namespace root once JDK
  ! classes can be imported directly (e.g. a future `import jvm
  ! "java.util.regex.Pattern"` for reflective FFI) — see
  ! docs/jips/jvm-backend.md for the full design rationale.
//]
annotation extern(owner: String, member: String, desc: String, kind: String)
